When a new proxy is configured in a repository, and p2phttp is serving that
repository, it will not notice the new proxy, and so won't know how to
serve its UUID, until it gets restarted.

When serving a directory with multiple repositories, p2phttp is able to
deal with a new repository being added. So maybe it also should be able to
deal with a new proxy being configured? 

This would entail making updateRepos scan for new proxies, basically.
Then when a UUID that is not known is requested, it would rescan. Seems
doable. --[[Joey]]
